 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 544277,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p><img src=\"exercises/media/da8897bdd047afff.jpg\" alt=\"The illustration shows a hormone crossing the cellular membrane and attaching to the NR/HSP complex. The complex dissociates, releasing the heat shock protein and a NR/hormone complex. The complex dimerizes, enters the nucleus, and attaches to an HRE element on DNA, triggering transcription of certain genes.\"></p>\n<p>Examine the illustration provided. Determine what kind of hormone is undergoing binding in this figure and describe the evidence in the figure that supports your answer.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1069777,
     "content_html": "A lipid-derived hormone is undergoing binding; this is evident because it is fat insoluble and therefore able to bind to receptors on the outer surface of the plasma membrane."
    },
    {
     "id": 1069778,
     "content_html": "A lipid-derived hormone is undergoing binding; this is evident because it is fat soluble and therefore able to pass through the cell membrane to reach intracellular receptors."
    },
    {
     "id": 1069779,
     "content_html": "A polypeptide-derived hormone is undergoing binding; this is evident because it is fat soluble and therefore able to pass through the cell membrane to reach intracellular receptors."
    },
    {
     "id": 1069780,
     "content_html": "A polypeptide-derived hormone is undergoing binding; this is evident because it is fat insoluble and therefore binds to receptors on the outer surface of the plasma membrane."
    }
   ],
